| footer            = [[Composting]] within [[agricultural systems]] capitalizes upon the natural services of nutrient recycling in ecosystems. [[Bacteria]], [[fungi]], [[insects]], [[earthworms]], [[Hemiptera|bugs]], and other creatures dig and digest the compost into fertile soil. The minerals and nutrients in the soil are recycled back into the production of crops.
